> **About `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` references below:** that env var resolves at skill-invocation time inside the plugin (to the plugin's installed root). When you see it in this doc, it's the symbolic path the plugin uses internally. The corresponding browsable URLs are linked above and throughout. You don't need to set the env var yourself — it's plugin-side machinery.

## How `flow` drives this project (the mechanism, not just the contract)

Three layers, in order of decreasing strength:

### 1. The rule layer (two different mechanisms — don't conflate them)

**Plugin-shipped rules are model-invoked**, not path-activated. They ship as skills at `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` with `user-invocable: false`, because a Claude Code plugin **cannot ship `.claude/rules/*.md` at all** — `rules/` is not a plugin component. Their descriptions are always in Claude's context; Claude loads the body when the description matches what it is doing. So they are **reliable-ish, not deterministic**: no glob guarantees them.

| Rule-skill | Claude should load it when | Enforces |
|---|---|---|
| `general` | Opening a non-trivial request, writing/editing a plan, committing, opening a PR, absorbing new scope, deciding to auto-advance into `/flow:ship` | Workflow discipline, scope, autonomy guardrails, "never merge" |
| `plan-discipline` | Writing, editing, or reviewing a plan; declaring acceptance criteria; choosing a mode | Required plan fields (mode, goal, scope in/out, spec-walk, confidence verdicts) + LOW = automatic human gate |
| `documentation` | Adding a history entry, synthesizing a correction into a feedback entry, updating roadmap/spec | Format rules (history entry shape, FB-XXXX entry shape, memory entry shape) |
| `exploration` | Finishing code or UI work, before `/flow:ship` | Grep this project's `roadmap.md § Exploration` for `Surfaces when:` triggers matching the file you're editing |

**Project-side rules ARE path-activated** — `.claude/rules/*.md` with `paths:` frontmatter is the mechanism that genuinely fires on a file read, and this project owns these files:

| Rule | Loads on | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `safety.md` | safety-critical paths declared in its `paths:` frontmatter — see that file for the current list | Read recent git log before modifying; never silently downgrade error handling; flag SAFETY in commits + history.md |
| `ui.md` (UI projects only) | UI file edits | Read `design-language.md` first; use tokens, not raw values; WCAG 2.1 AA baseline |
| `dev-server.md` (UI projects only) | UI file edits | Surface dev URL via `/link` after UI changes |

**Which layer is load-bearing, honestly.** Your own `.claude/rules/` fire deterministically on a path match — that is the enforcement layer you can rely on. The plugin's four are guidance Claude pulls in by judgment; treat them as raising the floor, not as a gate. If a rule genuinely must fire every time, put it in `.claude/rules/` here, or use a `PreToolUse` hook — Claude Code treats all of this as *context, not enforced configuration*.

> **Why this section is worded so carefully.** From flow v1.33.0 to v1.49.0 this table claimed the four plugin rules auto-loaded on path matches. They loaded for **nobody** — `paths:` on a `SKILL.md` narrows a description-driven activation rather than triggering one, and the descriptions said "path-activated only", which told Claude not to invoke them. A `/flow:doctor` check reported `[PASS]` over it for twenty releases by verifying **registration** and calling it **activation**. Fixed in v1.53.0 (FB-0124).

### 2. Skill auto-invocation (probabilistic — fires on description match)

`/flow:*` skills auto-trigger when phrases in their `description:` field match the conversation. Examples:

- After writing a plan → `/flow:critique-plan` (description: "Critique the most recent plan for scope drift, spec violation, internal incoherence")
- After completing implementation → `/flow:staff-review` (description: "Reviews the workspace's pending changes from four parallel staff-level perspectives")
- After saying "ship it" / "wrap this up" → `/flow:ship`

Not guaranteed to fire — model invocation is probabilistic. Type `/flow:<skill-name>` explicitly when you want certainty.

### 3. `/flow:ship` Step 1.0 assumption surface (after-the-fact — fires at ship time)

When you invoke `/flow:ship`, the pipeline's first action prints the workflow steps it ASSUMES already ran (Step 2 `/flow:critique-plan`, Step 6 `/simplify`, Step 7 `/flow:staff-review`). This is **informational only — doesn't gate** — but it surfaces silent skips so you notice the short-circuit at ship time rather than weeks later. Even on docs-only PRs, the discipline holds; see `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/docs/workflow.md` Step 2 + Step 6 "even on docs-only" notes.

After the assumption surface, `/flow:ship` runs hard pre-flight gates (Step 1a stale-base, Step 1.5 gh+jq fail-fast, etc.) that DO block on failure.

### What's NOT enforced today (honest gaps)

- **No Stop hook** that fails a session if `/flow:critique-plan` was skipped on a plan. The user can technically execute against an un-critiqued plan. Workflow.md's "Run on EVERY plan" qualifier captures the discipline, but enforcement is your own `.claude/rules/` + `/flow:ship` Step 1.0 surface, not a hard hook (the plugin's four rule-skills are model-invoked, so they cannot enforce anything). v1.x autonomous-routines work will add Stop hooks for this class.
- **No scope-check on Edit|Write** outside a plan's declared `files_touched`. Same v1.x scope.

## Docs

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `core-docs/spec.md` | Product vision, problem, solution, feature table, open questions |
| `core-docs/plan.md` | Current focus, active work items, handoff notes |
| `core-docs/roadmap.md` | Horizons (Now / Next / Later) + § Exploration |
| `core-docs/history.md` | Per-PR decision log: what + why + tradeoffs |
| `core-docs/feedback.md` | User feedback synthesized to rules (FB-XXXX) |
| `core-docs/design-language.md` | (UI projects) Tokens, axioms, components, motion — read before any UI change |
| `core-docs/visual-history.html` | (UI projects) Durable visual record — the picture companion to `history.md`; curated, reverse-chronological. Created-on-first-write + grown by `/flow:ship` Step 5c; never hand-edit the markers. |

## Quality bar

- **Polished over partial.** Every visible control does its job. Wire-vs-defer: if the gap is < 1 day, wire it; else remove the visible affordance and capture in roadmap.
- **Scope expansion is additive.** Ship the smallest polished form first.
- **No false affordances.** A button that doesn't work is a bug equivalent to a crash.

## Verify setup

In a Claude Code session at this project's root:

```
/flow:doctor
```

PASS / FAIL / WARN per check. Each FAIL prints the fix command. If `/flow:doctor` doesn't surface in your session, the plugin isn't enabled — re-run `/plugin install flow@flow` or check `.claude/settings.json`'s `enabledPlugins` entry.

